## Common Security Risks

Understanding how websites work helps identify:

- SQL Injection
- Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)
- Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF)
- Authentication Weaknesses
- Session Management Issues
- Insecure Direct Object References (IDOR)

## Why This Matters for Pentesting

Web application penetration testing focuses on understanding how websites function and identifying weaknesses in:

- Authentication
- Authorization
- Input Validation
- Session Handling
- Data Processing

